// Fixture for cratestack#806's floor raise: a `Bytes`-carrying model on
// `transport rpc`, which is the one configuration where a generated
// client actually depends on `@cratestack/cbor` (REST has no codec seam,
// so `rest-runtime.ts.j2` never imports it).
//
// Deliberately separate from `bytes_round_trip.cstack`, which
// `tests/bytes_round_trip.rs` uses: that fixture is REST-transport and
// asserts through `vitest` against `JSON.stringify`-based bodies, so it
// never touches the native codec at all — which is exactly why the
// byte-string defect #806 describes could ship without any test in this
// crate noticing.
//
// `Int[]` is included alongside `Bytes` on purpose. The two are
// indistinguishable at the TypeScript type level and were historically
// confusable on the wire, so a test that only looked at `Bytes` could not
// prove the codec was discriminating rather than coincidentally right.

transport rpc

model Attachment {
  id Cuid @id @default(cs_cuid())
  label String
  payload Bytes
  checksums Int[]

  @@allow("create", true)
  @@allow("list", true)
}
